# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values marked REQUIRED. Everything
# else works as it stands. The README describes each step under "Connecting
# Facebook".
#
# .env holds the keys to the Page's chat. Keep it on the machine that runs the
# assistant, and nowhere else. It is not committed to git.

# --- Facebook ------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. The number of your app at https://developers.facebook.com, shown at
# the top of the app's dashboard.
FB_APP_ID=

# REQUIRED. The app's secret: App settings > Basic > App secret > Show.
FB_APP_SECRET=

# REQUIRED. The token of the Page, from the app's dashboard: Use cases >
# Customize > Messenger API Settings > 2. Generate access tokens > "Generate"
# next to the Page. One more step is done by hand in the same place, once the
# assistant runs: "Add Subscriptions" (README, "Connecting the Page").
# "pnpm fb:check" says whether Facebook accepts the token and what it may do.
FB_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# The HTTPS address under which Facebook reaches this program from the
# internet, without a path: the assistant registers it with Facebook by itself.
# Not needed with "pnpm start --tunnel", which is for trying out.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://assistant.example.com

# The Page the assistant answers for, when the token could be for several.
# "pnpm fb:check" shows the id.
# FB_PAGE_ID=

# true once Facebook has approved the app for "Human Agent": people of the
# team can then write from the dashboard for 7 days after a customer's last
# message instead of 24 hours.
# FB_HUMAN_AGENT_TAG=false

# The version of Facebook's interface. Facebook retires a version about two
# years after it appears.
# FB_GRAPH_VERSION=v27.0

# Only if you enter the webhook in Facebook's dashboard by hand instead of
# letting the assistant register it: the "verify token" you enter there.
# FB_VERIFY_TOKEN=

# --- Dashboard -----------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. The password of the dashboard, at least 8 characters. The dashboard
# shows customers' names, phone numbers and chats.
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

# Where the dashboard listens. 127.0.0.1 means: only from this machine. To open
# it from a phone or another computer, put it behind HTTPS (see the README)
# rather than changing the host.
# DASHBOARD_HOST=127.0.0.1
# DASHBOARD_PORT=3400

# The address under which the team reaches the dashboard, put into the
# messages the team gets on Messenger. Leave empty for no link.
# DASHBOARD_URL=https://desk.example.com

# --- What Facebook calls -------------------------------------------------------
# Where the part that is open to the internet listens: the address Facebook
# calls, and the privacy notice. PUBLIC_URL must lead here. With the same
# number as DASHBOARD_PORT, both are served from one port.
# WEBHOOK_HOST=127.0.0.1
# WEBHOOK_PORT=3401

# --- The team ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Team members who get a Messenger message from the Page when a booking comes
# in or a chat needs a person: their ids as the dashboard shows them under
# Chats ("Facebook id"), separated by commas. Facebook passes these messages on
# only to someone who wrote to the Page within the last 24 hours.
# STAFF_THREAD_IDS=

# --- Behaviour -----------------------------------------------------------------
# How long the assistant waits for a customer to finish writing before it answers.
# REPLY_WAIT_SECONDS=2.5

# How long the assistant stays out of a chat after a person of the team wrote
# in it, or after it passed the chat to a person.
# STAFF_PAUSE_HOURS=12

# After this many answers in one chat within an hour the assistant stops and
# calls a person: it is probably talking to another automatic account.
# MAX_REPLIES_PER_HOUR=40

# --- Files ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the assistant says and sells.
# BUSINESS_FILE=config/business.ts

# Where the database (bookings, chats) is kept. Back this folder up.
# DATA_DIR=./var

# debug, info, warn, error or silent
# LOG_LEVEL=info
